<title>NORWAY: Nycomed rises further in heavy trade.</title>
<headline>Nycomed rises further in heavy trade.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Norwegian pharmaceuticals group Nycomed ASA continued to climb to new highs on Wednesday in heavy trade, a day after it announced merger plans with Britain's Amersham International Plc.</p>
<p>At 1200 GMT, Nycomed's A stock stood at a year high of 139 crowns, a gain of almost five percent, while the Bs had risen two percent to 132.50 crowns.</p>
<p>Turnover in the Oslo-based company accounted for 407 million crowns of the bourse's turnover so far of 843 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
